==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|bull<id:male cattle>|pen|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-bullpen.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An enclosed area used to hold [[bull]]s.
#: {{cot|en|cowpen}}
#: {{ux|en|Magnus and Big Dick are over in the '''bullpen''', ready for tonight's rodeo.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q579478}} {{lb|en|baseball}} An enclosed area for [[pitcher]]s to warm up in during a game.
#: {{ux|en|After that hit, there is activity in the '''bullpen'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Billy Witz|title=Camaraderie of Wrigley Field Bullpens Is Tangled Amid the Ivy|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/07/sports/baseball/wrigley-field-bullpens-renovations.html|date=07-05-2017|passage=Now the '''bullpens''' are hidden away underneath the bleachers, out of sight and sound.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240916032453/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/07/sports/baseball/wrigley-field-bullpens-renovations.html|archivedate=16 September 2024}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Greg Jewett|title=Bullpen report: Porter Hodge enters Cubs’ circle of trust, Mason Miller cools down and more|url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5618689/2024/07/05/mlb-bullpen-fantasy-baseball-mason-miller-2/|date=05-07-2024|passage=Even though the Phillies '''bullpen''' has been a strength, it may be shopping for a veteran capable of handling the ninth inning.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240916033955/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5618689/2024/07/05/mlb-bullpen-fantasy-baseball-mason-miller-2/|archivedate=16 September 2024}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The relief pitchers of a team collectively.
#: {{ux|en|Their '''bullpen''' is worn out after yesterday's doubleheader where both games went 12 innings.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A place for someone or something to get ready.
#: {{ux|en|If this team of consultants fails, I have another warming up in the '''bullpen'''.}}
# An open seating arrangement where project teams can communicate openly with minimal effort.
#: {{ux|en|We have our sales team in a '''bullpen''' setup to keep their energy flowing.}}
# {{lb|en|US|military slang}} A [[military prison]] or its [[enclose|enclosing]] [[stockade]].<ref>{{R:en:Lighter:1972|page=24}}</ref>

